{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/888259-reading-aspirations","id":888259,"title":"Reading Aspirations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-11T08:59:01-07:00","id":888259,"title":"Reading Aspirations","content":"There are a couple of different ways that I am aware of for the various splats to find out the aspirations of characters in game. I think this is a <i>really </i>cool approach to this kind of power. However, one of the suggestions when the book talks about creating aspirations is for you to include one that is something that <b>you as a player</b> want for your character, even if that isn't something that the character wants. If I have an NPC Beast use Eye of Heaven or Mage use Mind magic, what are they supposed to make of these kinds of aspirations? Do you just pretend like they don't exist? Do they see them and interpret them as a sort of destiny?<br /> <br /> It's not a big deal, I just thought of it and went &quot;Huh.&quot; How would you handle this? Maybe in practice people don't really do these kinds of aspirations so it doesn't really matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:15:36-07:00","id":888271,"title":"","content":"You're assumed to put those powers in use against NPCs, and their aspirations aren't, let's call them Out of Character.<br /> <br /> If you do aim that at PCs, assume it's the subconscious. Could be really fucked up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:28:16-07:00","id":888282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/888259-reading-aspirations?p=888271#post888271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're assumed to put those powers in use against NPCs, and their aspirations aren't, let's call them Out of Character.<br /> <br /> If you do aim that at PCs, assume it's the subconscious. Could be really fucked up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess if you use these kind of powers on the PCs then it incentivizes them to not have things that are important to them as aspirations, for fear that their enemies will find out. It's kind of a weird situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:35:53-07:00","id":888288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/888259-reading-aspirations?p=888282#post888282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I guess if you use these kind of powers on the PCs then it incentivizes them to not have things that are important to them as aspirations, for fear that their enemies will find out. It's kind of a weird situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about you, but I want enemies to know what's important to my character: If I'm an immortal vampire protected by vampire politics, attacking my Touchstones or finding out what I want is the best way to put me in an awkward (read: dramatic) situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:39:46-07:00","id":888291,"title":"","content":"You could interpret them as hidden desires, buried in their subconscious and they secretly want them to happen but consciously oppose the idea. I tend to do these sort of aspirations and I usually just make them fit the character in some fashion, like if they're a career thief who is exceedingly good at what they do, they don't want to get caught consciously, but in the back of their head there's this voice that sometimes just wishes it'd happen so they could see what it's like to lose for once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T10:55:02-07:00","id":888372,"title":"","content":"Or that those Out of Characters Aspirations are more like... Destiny of character. Because, in reality, they <i>are</i> Destiny - players is pushing character in to this situations to get his Beat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}